1
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,320
I've finished the revisions.
I'll email it to you in a bit.

3
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:47,960
Bye.

4
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,640
Sir, your package.

5
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,640
Thanks.

6
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:05,800
<i>Apologize again with thanks.</i>

7
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,600
Here is the billing statement.

8
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:37,200
Among the new products, the shampoo
and body wash are selling pretty well.

9
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:43,840
Sunscreen and serum sales
are also increasing.

10
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,120
Okay. Got it.

11
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,560
Xu Chi.

12
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:05,160
I told the Research
to send you home to rest.

13
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,360
Why are you still here?

14
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,640
I'd just be idle at home.
Might as well work.

15
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:10,560
Ms. Lin, you're done with your meeting?

16
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,320
I just ran into Mr. Pi.

17
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,240
I told him I asked to help out
with the Conference Team.

18
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:24,440
Getting to network
with some industry heavyweights

19
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,360
is totally worth it.

20
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,360
Good to know.

21
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,920
Mr. Pi is giving a speech
at the summit tomorrow afternoon.

22
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:39,840
I'll bring you along.

23
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,920
You can meet some people in the circle.

24
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,960
Alright. Thanks, Ms. Lin.

25
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:58,520
Homegrown innovative companies
need to handle both sides at once.

26
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,280
Survival in the short term

27
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,080
and strategic positioning
for the long run.

28
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,160
Get back to the roots
of innovation and value creation.

29
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:10,520
Differentiating globally
while sharpening our competitive edge.

30
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:13,480
Multinationals are required to rethink

31
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,840
their business objectives
and strategies for the China market.

32
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:20,280
Balance risks and opportunities,
and be more proactive in finding ways

33
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:23,520
to turn China's unique strengths
into global value.

34
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:27,000
For example, product pipelines,
business models,

35
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,000
R&amp;D capabilities, and talent.

36
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,200
Thank you all.

37
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,160
Alright. Thank you, Mr. Pi.

38
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,840
Next, let's welcome Mr. Ye Xinzhi,

39
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,640
partner at C&amp;C Consulting, to the stage.

40
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,560
Let's welcome Mr. Ye.

41
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,080
Hello, everyone.

42
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,480
I'm Ye Xinzhi from C&amp;C Consulting.

43
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,800
Your presentation earlier was brilliant.

44
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,400
I learned so much from you.

45
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,160
Mr. Chen. Mr. Li.

46
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,760
-Long time no see.
-Long time no see.

47
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,800
Hello. I'm Xu Chi from Maxmise Consulting.

48
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,840
-Hello.
-Which part did you find most interesting?

49
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,200
Sure. Right?

50
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:13,800
Long time no see.

51
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,840
How have you been?

52
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,640
Thanks, Ms. Lin.

53
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,600
New-quality productive forces
are a hot topic right now.

54
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,440
Our entire team
will be paying more attention to it.

55
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:23,400
So whenever you get the chance,

56
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,720
you should connect more
with the leaders in this space.

57
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,600
Got it.

58
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,760
Look.

59
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,960
This is Mr. Yan, President
of the Yunshang Internet Association.

60
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,120
I'll head over first.

61
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,720
-Mr. Yan.
-Hey.

62
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,800
-Long time no see.
-Long time no see.

63
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:38,840
Been busy lately?

64
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,680
Yeah. Always busy.

65
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,200
Why didn't you reply to my messages?

66
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:46,240
I wanted to ask you
about the Suhu AI industry cluster before,

67
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,920
but you never got back to me.

68
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,080
I figured you must have just forgotten
with how busy you are.

69
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,640
You bet.

70
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,080
‎2025 EMPOWERING WITH DIGITAL
‎LEADING THE FUTURE

71
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,280
Let me introduce you.

72
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,400
This is my new colleague, Xu Chi.

73
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,760
-Hi.
-Hello.

74
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,360
Mr. Yan.

75
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,000
I've got some inside info.

76
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,200
This morning,
Wanghu Pavilion Restaurant upstairs

77
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,120
just got in some top-quality hairtail.

78
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,080
The best delicacy.

79
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,360
Really?

80
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,120
Since we're already here,
why don't we head upstairs and chat?

81
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:13,240
Sure.

82
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,640
Come on.

83
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,400
Come on.

84
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,000
Hello. Could you tell me
where the Chinese restaurant is?

85
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,600
-Over there.
-Thanks.

86
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:40,960
What's wrong?

87
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,360
I'm fine.

88
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,960
Did you drink on your own,
or were you pressured into it?

89
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,080
Take a guess.

90
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,120
You'd better watch your back.

91
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,800
You think I just got propositioned?

92
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,800
What really happened?

93
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,640
Someone's out to get me.

94
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,320
Mr. Yan, you're the man.

95
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,160
The summit's got every private room
booked today,

96
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,040
but the moment I dropped your name,

97
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,600
-one opened up.
-Really?

98
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,840
The fish will be here soon.
Let's wait a bit.

99
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:25,960
Sure thing.

100
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,640
Let me take this call.

101
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,520
Hello, Mr. Zhao.

102
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:38,400
You really need to come to me for this?
Can't you handle it yourself?

103
00:08:38,919 --> 00:08:39,960
Gotta go.

104
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:41,960
<i>Be sharp.</i>

105
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:43,799
-<i>Mr. Yan likes being flattered.</i>
-Try this.

106
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,280
-<i>He hates awkward silences.</i>
-Thanks.

107
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,200
Mr. Yan.

108
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:53,400
You just said future policies
will regulate AI misuse.

109
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,840
How strict will that be?

110
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,240
Very strict.

111
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:00,000
In our lingo, "Regulatory action
needs to hit the mark and hit hard."

112
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:02,640
Like when you were a kid,
didn't listen to your dad,

113
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:05,400
and got spanked.

114
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:09,440
Mr. Yan, you really have a sense of humor.

115
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:12,440
My belly hurts from laughing.

116
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,920
Don't hurt the baby.

117
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,520
If anything happened to the little one,

118
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,440
-I'd never forgive myself.
-Not at all.

119
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,440
My bad.

120
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:19,720
I'll take a drink as an apology.

121
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,120
Where's the wine?

122
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,480
-Excuse me.
-Hello.

123
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,480
Come on.

124
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:29,160
Bring me your best wine. Quick.

125
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,120
-Got it.
-Hurry up.

126
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,920
Good fish calls for good wine.

127
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,280
-Right?
-Yeah.

128
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,640
One second. Wait a moment. Here.

129
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,240
-Let's try something else.
-Okay.

130
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,560
Let's toast.

131
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,120
Mr. Yan, I'm so happy I totally forgot.

132
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,480
I can't have any alcohol right now.

133
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,440
But today we've got Xu as backup.
No worries.

134
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:52,080
Ms. Lin, I told you
I'm allergic to alcohol.

135
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,040
So what do we do now?

136
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,720
I'm pregnant.
Can't have me drinking, right?

137
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,960
Don't worry. Just take it slow.

138
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,280
Build up your tolerance.

139
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,320
Exactly.

140
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,440
That's how everything works.

141
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,680
First time's awkward, second time's easy.

142
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,520
Mr. Yan, I really don't drink.

143
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,040
Cheers.

144
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,320
-Drink up.
-Mr. Yan, I don't--

145
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,080
Come on.

146
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,360
There you go.

147
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,320
Right?

148
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,240
My superior set me up.

149
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,480
I had to drink way too much.

150
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,400
I kept pinching myself
while trying to find a way out.

151
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,320
Then she went to the restroom
and left her phone behind.

152
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:38,480
Her husband kept calling her.

153
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,720
I was worried it was urgent,
so I answered.

154
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,480
The next thing,

155
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,400
her husband showed up furious.

156
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,640
Mr. Yan got a face full of wine.
That was the end of that dinner.

157
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,880
Are you expecting me
to praise you or chew you out?

158
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,640
She's pregnant.

159
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,000
So just because she's pregnant,

160
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
I'm supposed to take it lying down?

161
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,640
Look,

162
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:09,200
if someone treats me with respect,
I return it tenfold,

163
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:12,040
but if they cross me, I'm not a pushover.

164
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:16,720
You've got a strong sense
of both defense and offense.

165
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:22,360
Seems like your days at Maxmise

166
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,640
aren't easy.

167
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,120
I've been more than decent to her.

168
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:28,720
I did everything I could.
I put up with everything I could!

169
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,920
Out of all the new hires,
I'm the best and the hardest-working.

170
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,160
What more does she want?

171
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,600
She's a woman too.

172
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:35,000
How could she come up
with such a dirty trick?

173
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,280
Because she feels threatened.

174
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,400
She's afraid you'll replace her.

175
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:42,080
No way! She's my mentor.

176
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,680
I'm just an intern business analyst.

177
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:48,440
People who don't feel secure
often lose out

178
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,600
on a lot of opportunities at work.

179
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,280
Killing off a threatening young lion early

180
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,200
is the most common move among adult lions.

181
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,080
One bottle of water bought you
20 minutes of career advice.

182
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,280
Pretty good deal.

183
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,720
You want me to walk you down
and call you a cab?

184
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:16,240
I wasn't in the bathroom throwing up
because my stomach hurt.

185
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:19,200
Just trying to limit the damage
from all that drinking.

186
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,400
Still, be careful.

187
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,960
Take care of yourself.

188
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,320
Mr. Ye.

189
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,400
Why did you leave P&amp;J?

190
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:36,960
When I went back
to return your sunglasses,

191
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:39,200
I found out you'd already left P&amp;J.

192
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,480
OPERATIONS DEPARTMENT
YE XINZHI, DIRECTOR OF OPERATIONS

193
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,920
I really wanted to thank you in person

194
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,200
for your advice back then.

195
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,320
No need for that.

196
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:00,880
I was just saying something offhand.

197
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:04,400
Congratulations on making it into Maxmise,
just like you wanted.

198
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,360
Consultants have a practice.

199
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,920
Sometimes we take a gap at a corporate
just to stay connected to the market.

200
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,360
When you met me back then,
I happened to be gapping at P&amp;J.

201
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:16,080
C&amp;C Consulting
and Maxmise are competitors.

202
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,560
This hotel is packed
with summit attendees.

203
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,920
People might get the wrong idea.

204
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,920
You should head back. Good luck.

205
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:48,200
XU CHI LOVES MOM

206
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,560
Mom, look.

207
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:01,680
I love coming
to Grandma's apartment in Beijing.

208
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,840
-Mom. I want some tanghulu.
-Let's go!

209
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:39,680
NO. 92, YONG'AN ROAD

210
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,000
<i>Lin Long.</i>

211
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,120
Why are you so late?

212
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,880
You look worn out.

213
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:07,920
-You threw wine in his face…
-You're pregnant. Why were you drinking?

214
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,600
I… I wasn't drinking.

215
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,400
-It was just normal business talk.
-It is not normal!

216
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,880
You're impossible!

217
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,960
Don't walk away. Come back
and finish what you were saying!

218
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,560
I'd say just get a cat.

219
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:18,920
At least it gives you emotional support.

220
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,040
A cat works too, but I would still date.

221
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:24,240
And in terms of structure and process,
we need to analyze everything.

222
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,400
I'm heading off.

223
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,240
Morning, Ms. Lin.

224
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,120
Morning, Sha Sha.

225
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,440
Morning.

226
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:34,040
Mr. Pi is asking about the progress
on the Bolo Culture project.

227
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,680
Did you set up a meeting time
with them this afternoon?

228
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,160
Already done. Don't worry.

229
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,200
Bolo Culture is very happy
with Ms. Lin's proposal.

230
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,640
You…

231
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,640
Why did you answer
my phone for me yesterday?

232
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,240
I'm sorry.

233
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,680
You told me to drink with Mr. Yan.

234
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:15,680
-I had no idea your husband had a temper.
-Lower your voice.

235
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:16,800
Keep your voice down.

236
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,040
You want to blow things up, do you?

237
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:24,160
Let me make this clear.
Know what you should do

238
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:25,480
and what you shouldn't.

239
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,640
People who lack security miss out

240
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,240
on a lot of opportunities
in the workplace.

241
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:35,800
Killing off a threatening young lion early
is the most common move among adult lions.

242
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,680
Got it.

243
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:41,080
What I should do is get
the Yuanming proposal done for you.

244
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,120
What's wrong?

245
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,240
That girl is absolutely awful!
I completely misjudged her!

246
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,599
Calm down.

247
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:12,000
Your performance
has ranked number one for years.

248
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:13,599
Nothing to worry about.

249
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,800
It's just a newbie trying to stand out.
We've seen plenty of those over the years.

250
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,599
Just don't let her shine on any projects.

251
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,359
She'll leave on her own
in a couple of days.

252
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,120
Once we get to Bolo Culture,

253
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:35,680
don't say a single word
without my permission.

254
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,560
-Got it?
-Got it.

255
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,760
Regarding the organizational efficiency
development after your acquisition

256
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:49,840
of Qingyi Literature,

257
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:53,680
Maxmise recommends a focused integration
of copyright content and design.

258
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,600
MR. SHEN, BOLO CULTURE

259
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,560
Maxmise suggests establishing

260
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,240
a dedicated efficiency improvement team,
Exercise Evaluation Team, also called EET.

261
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:00,760
EET serves as the key driver
for the entire cost-reduction project,

262
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,640
using data-driven methods

263
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,400
to push deep collaboration
across organizations

264
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:06,080
and restructure cost frameworks.

265
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,000
At the top level,

266
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:09,000
the steering committee acts as sponsor,
providing strategic direction.

267
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:11,720
At the execution level,
the EET lead consolidates resources,

268
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:12,640
extending downward

269
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,480
into five functional areas,
including process optimization,

270
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,800
data analysis, HR coordination,

271
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:18,160
finance coordination,
and IT system integration,

272
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:20,520
-forming an end-to-end closed loop.
-Mr. Shen.

273
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,920
Something doesn't feel right to you?

274
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,800
Actually, yes.

275
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:31,400
Ms. Lin, can you just tell me straight up
what we actually need to do

276
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:34,560
to get the veteran Qingyi employees
to integrate into our group,

277
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:37,000
fall in line, and stay motivated
at the same time?

278
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,680
-Give me something useful.
-Useful stuff…

279
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,680
Coming up.

280
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,080
The biggest problem

281
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,840
with Qingyi Literature
is its chaotic internal management.

282
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,840
‎ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE: OVERLY FLAT

283
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,200
It's been around for a while,

284
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,840
but--

285
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,240
Ms. Lin.

286
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:07,840
You want to take a break?

287
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,760
Yeah, yeah. Let's go downstairs
and grab some coffee.

288
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:19,040
Seriously, is that all they've got?

289
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:22,440
A few PowerPoint slides and some plans,
and they dare charge us eight figures?

290
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,200
What year is this?

291
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,920
These consulting firms
still think we're easy money.

292
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:27,880
Exactly.

293
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:32,520
Let me give you two numbers.

294
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:37,760
One-third of Fortune 500
board chairs have a background

295
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:39,160
in management consulting.

296
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,560
That's true.

297
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:42,720
A lot of traditional consulting firms
are just big talkers.

298
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:47,440
But what I value is Maxmise's status
as a top global firm

299
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,480
and the management expertise,
operating models,

300
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,320
and databases they bring to the table.

301
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,920
Those are real battle-tested assets

302
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,600
they built up over decades
across dozens of countries.

303
00:19:56,680 --> 00:20:00,720
We're taking our IP commercial and global.
Who else are we going to rely on?

304
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,480
You?

305
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:04,360
You guys?

306
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:06,840
You're going to go to Rio, to Osaka,

307
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:09,680
country by country doing market research?

308
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,040
By the time you're done,
it'll be too late.

309
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,120
But their proposal just now
really wasn't good enough.

310
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,080
Then we won't choose them.

311
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:20,280
Besides Maxmise, there are other firms.

312
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,680
Let's use this project
to test the waters first.

313
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:24,280
Warm water.

314
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:29,440
Why did you speak
without my permission just now?

315
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:30,600
What did I tell you before we came?

316
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,960
They were all zoning out.

317
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,640
Using a question to recapture
the client's attention

318
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:36,320
and pull them back into the discussion.

319
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,920
That's a proposal technique you taught me.

320
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:40,800
I'm warning you one last time. Just one.

321
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,160
If you want to get through
your internship smoothly,

322
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,600
stay in your lane.

323
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,320
Mr. Shen.

324
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,920
Sorry about that.

325
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,760
No worries.
You're in a special situation after all.

326
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:58,080
But I do suggest
that if you're really not feeling well,

327
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,640
maybe take some time off.

328
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,680
Work isn't more important than your baby.

329
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,200
Xu Chi, what are you doing?

330
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,720
Wait, what do you mean?

331
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:29,720
Mr. Shen, you asked
how to get Qingyi employees

332
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,320
to listen, work hard,
and integrate, right?

333
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:34,840
The solution is to use money to bring
in a new cohort of employees.

334
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,360
Qingyi has been around for over 20 years.

335
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:43,640
Their average employee age is around 45.

336
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,520
They're used to family-style
workshop management.

337
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:47,400
Getting them to quickly integrate

338
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:49,200
into Bolo Culture,
which has only existed for five years,

339
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,840
is as hard as me suddenly becoming

340
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,040
a top web novelist making 50,000 a month.

341
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:58,360
Since your company isn't short on cash,
and all you care about is Qingyi's IPs,

342
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,440
why not start fresh?

343
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,400
Keep the senior executives for now.

344
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,000
Let all other former
Qingyi employees leave

345
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:05,960
with the market's best severance package
of 2N plus 10.

346
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:09,320
That way, regular employees can retire.

347
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,200
It also cleans up the mess quickly.

348
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:13,880
And it boosts
Bolo Culture's brand reputation.

349
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,920
Three birds with one stone.

350
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:22,720
Actually, I've always felt
that a lean, boutique HR structure

351
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,680
is one of your company's
greatest strengths.

352
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:27,760
So the follow-up reform plan
should also revolve around that.

353
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,440
Tell me more.

354
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:32,440
Let's save the suspense
for after the proposal meeting.

355
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:34,160
Sorry, Ms. Lin,

356
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:35,200
I don't like suspense.

357
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:39,200
-Go on.
-Alright.

358
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,040
Based on our preliminary research,

359
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:47,400
we found that Bolo Culture's
incentive system is actually quite solid,

360
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:50,400
but it has three coexisting pay models,

361
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,920
namely position-based,
skill-based, and performance-based.

362
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,360
It's overly mixed.

363
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,960
So here we suggest…

364
00:22:58,720 --> 00:22:59,920
Thank you both for today.

365
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:02,560
Miss Xu, your proposal was excellent.

366
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,880
You're too kind.

367
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:07,280
Maxmise has always been committed
to providing our clients

368
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:08,880
with the highest quality
consulting services.

369
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:10,760
And of course, thank you too, Ms. Lin.

370
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:12,240
You have a great team.

371
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:16,000
Thanks for the compliment.

372
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:18,080
We'll get back to you soon.

373
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,760
-Looking forward to it.
-No need to see us out.

374
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,320
Happy now?

375
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,560
Had enough of the spotlight?

376
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:38,280
I helped salvage a project
that was about to fall through.

377
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:40,800
As a member of the team,
of course, I'm happy.

378
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,440
A member of the team?

379
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:45,840
Don't think I can't see it.

380
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:48,840
You joined Maxmise just to replace me.

381
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:54,040
Ms. Lin, you're overthinking it.

382
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:56,200
I'm just an intern analyst.

383
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:58,920
I wouldn't set replacing
a consultant two levels above me

384
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,280
as a goal.

385
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:03,400
You can fool others, but not me.

386
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,000
I'm really not lying to you.

387
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:07,680
Because my goal
isn't to replace you at all.

388
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:11,600
It's to become someone in this city
who can never be replaced.

389
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:31,400
Go on your own.

390
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:33,480
My car can't fit a dream that big.

391
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,480
Sha Sha, do you have a minute?

392
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,040
Come in.

393
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:52,360
I'd like to talk to you
about the Bolo Culture project.

394
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:56,080
That management team
is indeed a bit young.

395
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:57,000
Tough to handle.

396
00:24:57,080 --> 00:24:58,880
Luckily, I changed
the proposal on the fly.

397
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,080
They've given preliminary approval.

398
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,200
Take a look.

399
00:25:06,080 --> 00:25:09,080
But Xu Chi did something
absolutely ridiculous today.

400
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,120
She secretly pulled out

401
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:14,720
a stack of cash and tried to bribe
Bolo Culture's CEO.

402
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:17,240
You have no idea how awkward it was.

403
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:19,120
I can't even describe it.

404
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:20,720
Really?

405
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:24,680
Xu Chi is indeed a capable girl.

406
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:27,160
But that kind of behavior
violates business ethics,

407
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,600
and it's a huge red flag at Maxmise.

408
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:31,600
I don't think I'm suitable
to be her mentor anymore.

409
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:34,200
I suggest we terminate
her probation early.

410
00:25:36,040 --> 00:25:37,080
Is that really what you want?

411
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,840
That way, she can still go
to other companies.

412
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:45,120
Nice proposal.

413
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:49,520
But 20 minutes ago,
Xu Chi sent me one too.

414
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,400
Her thinking is exactly the same…

415
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:53,680
PRODUCER - LIN LONG, XU CHI

416
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:54,800
…as yours.

417
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:58,080
No-- Sha Sha, this--

418
00:25:58,160 --> 00:25:59,320
I can explain--

419
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,000
Do you think that's necessary, Lin Long?

420
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:03,080
You've been with me for so long.

421
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:06,400
I've never overlooked
your personality or your needs.

422
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:09,760
You thought Cindy poached
the Sato Pharmaceuticals project from you,

423
00:26:09,840 --> 00:26:12,320
so I immediately gave you
the Bolo Culture project.

424
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:15,360
Now you're pregnant and low on energy,

425
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:16,480
so I found you an assistant.

426
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,440
You picked Xu Chi yourself,

427
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,280
and she's the most capable
among this batch of new hires.

428
00:26:21,360 --> 00:26:24,040
I don't know what went wrong
in your communication,

429
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:26,440
but when it comes to teamwork,

430
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,080
she did better than you.

431
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:30,000
But she always acts on her own.

432
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:32,040
Does she even see me as her mentor?

433
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:34,400
She goes over my head on everything
without my approval.

434
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,400
Performance is the only thing
that matters.

435
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,600
You can't expect
to only ever have subordinates

436
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:40,920
who are less capable than you.

437
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:45,360
Whether you can manage them well
depends on your leadership.

438
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:47,600
The net you wove is too loose
to hold her down.

439
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:48,840
So she just slips
through the gaps and rises--

440
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:50,520
So this is all my fault then?

441
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,200
You're not in a good state today.

442
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,840
I suggest you take your leave immediately.

443
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:08,200
You like taking on work, don't you?
Then all of this is yours now.

444
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,480
Well done.

445
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:27,680
<i>Well done.</i>

446
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:31,520
BU TIANNA

447
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:37,920
<i>It's just a newbie trying to stand out.</i>
<i>We've seen plenty of those over the years.</i>

448
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,640
You thought she was a pushover.

449
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:42,920
She waited until everyone forgot,
then got her revenge.

450
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,760
She is more calculating than you.

451
00:27:45,360 --> 00:27:48,240
Xu Chi is clearly someone
who can really get things done.

452
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:50,440
If you piss off Mr. Pi because of her,

453
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:53,640
aren't you afraid
he'll give you a hard time at work?

454
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:55,120
I just ran into Mr. Pi.

455
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:58,360
I told him I asked to help out
with the Conference Team.

456
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:00,840
<i>Ms. Lin, you're overthinking it.</i>

457
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:03,240
I'm just an intern analyst.

458
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:06,000
I wouldn't set replacing
a consultant two levels above me

459
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:07,080
as a goal.

460
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:09,840
Performance is the only thing
that matters.

461
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:12,000
You can't expect
to only ever have subordinates

462
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,320
who are less capable than you.

463
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,680
Watch where you're going!

464
00:28:39,720 --> 00:28:40,840
Sorry about that.

465
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:44,200
My fault entirely.
We can do a fast-track insurance claim.

466
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:46,960
Ms. Lin?

467
00:28:48,320 --> 00:28:49,320
Mr. Shen?

468
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,000
-I'm really sorry. I--
-You're bleeding.

469
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:59,200
You're pregnant.
How could you drive so carelessly?

470
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:00,800
Is the baby okay?

471
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:04,120
-It's fine.
-You're hurt.

472
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:06,800
I'll take full responsibility.
I'll take you to the hospital.

473
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:14,640
Doctor, the fees are paid.

474
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:16,160
-Alright.
-How is she?

475
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,640
The wound isn't deep. No stitches needed.

476
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:18,920
Just clean it

477
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,840
and apply the medicine once a day
for three days straight.

478
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:23,080
The wound is in her hair.
It's not really noticeable.

479
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:25,120
Is the baby okay?

480
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,800
We ran all the tests. Everything's fine.

481
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,920
But I've warned her before.

482
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:31,240
I told her to make sure
she gets plenty of rest.

483
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:33,520
But this time I saw
that her heart rate is too fast.

484
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:35,520
It's worse than last time.

485
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,240
As the father,

486
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:38,800
you should come with her
for more prenatal checkups--

487
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:39,920
No, no. Doctor, that's not it.

488
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,120
He's just my business partner,
not the baby's father.

489
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,520
I'm definitely not her husband.

490
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:46,440
I'm her client.

491
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:49,560
I'll wait outside.

492
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:07,600
Sorry about earlier.

493
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:10,800
I barely thought it was a big deal.
Don't mention it.

494
00:30:13,600 --> 00:30:14,440
Thanks for driving me home.

495
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,840
Don't get the wrong idea.

496
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:21,240
It's just that you're pregnant.

497
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:23,600
If something happened to you,
I couldn't bear that responsibility.

498
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:27,640
You must be four or five months along?

499
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,600
When my sister was pregnant,

500
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:32,600
she was already on bed rest at this stage.

501
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:35,000
You're either running to our company

502
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:37,120
and standing for hours
giving presentations

503
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,360
or playing Fast &amp; Furious on your own.

504
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:42,560
Is it really worth working yourself
to the bone for your company?

505
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:46,400
That's just how we consultants are.

506
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,720
And Maxmise really values

507
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:50,800
-this Bolo Culture project…
-Alright, alright. Stop it.

508
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:53,880
It's just the two of us here.
No need for all that corporate flattery.

509
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,520
I'll give you a little inside scoop.
Your company has a good shot at this deal.

510
00:30:58,600 --> 00:31:02,520
So I suggest you just go home and rest up.

511
00:31:02,600 --> 00:31:05,360
Leave the rest to Miss Xu.

512
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:06,840
She can handle the follow-up.

513
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:08,080
Xu Chi?

514
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:12,800
That's not really appropriate. She… She's…

515
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,760
She's inexperienced,
and she just joined the company--

516
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:16,440
And you're so experienced?

517
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:19,160
Your proposal wasn't that great.

518
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:20,760
Full of clichés.

519
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:21,760
You think you can just
swap out a model template

520
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:23,240
and rip us off?

521
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:25,320
Think we're just some
dumb money waiting to be fleeced?

522
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:27,160
Xu Chi's proposal
was more interesting than yours--

523
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,240
Enough already!

524
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:30,440
What?

525
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,240
What's your problem?

526
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:37,480
Sorry. I've been feeling
a bit unstable emotionally.

527
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:45,200
Your pregnancy hormones
are all over the place.

528
00:31:45,280 --> 00:31:46,200
I get that.

529
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:48,200
But let me give you some advice.

530
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:51,520
Don't let this cost you clients,
cost you your boss,

531
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:53,160
and then cost you your husband.

532
00:31:53,240 --> 00:31:55,680
Then you've got nothing left.

533
00:31:55,760 --> 00:31:57,200
Game over. Got it?

534
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:22,800
FOOD DELIVERIES PLEASE LEAVE AT DOOR
TABLE ON THE LEFT

535
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:58,240
Okay. I'll have three.

536
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,160
I want two more.

537
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:01,360
-Impossible!
-What's making you guys so happy?

538
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:05,360
Ms. Sha. Xu Chi has been
the first one in the office

539
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:06,760
for 27 days straight.

540
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:09,200
We were just chatting.

541
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:11,600
Wondering if she can keep it up
through the whole internship.

542
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:25,600
Zhiwen.

543
00:33:27,440 --> 00:33:29,320
Zhiwen. The baby kicked.

544
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:30,880
Come listen.

545
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:42,320
Sha Sha.

546
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:48,640
I want to apologize
for my attitude yesterday.

547
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:49,760
I wasn't in a good place.

548
00:33:49,840 --> 00:33:53,000
I don't even know if it's the pregnancy.

549
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:56,360
I've been through everything
you're going through.

550
00:33:57,280 --> 00:34:01,120
Women make up less than a third
of the employees at Maxmise.

551
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:04,080
Helping you is helping myself.

552
00:34:07,120 --> 00:34:08,320
From now on,

553
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,120
I'll focus on the Yuanming project.

554
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:13,560
Let Xu Chi take over
the Bolo Culture project.

555
00:34:13,639 --> 00:34:14,800
I'll just oversee from behind.

556
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:17,920
That's the smart choice.

557
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:20,880
Nothing is more important
than your health.

558
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:25,199
Don't worry. When you come back,

559
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,800
your position and responsibilities
won't change.

560
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:28,280
That's my promise.

561
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:31,040
Thanks.

562
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:29,960
What's got you so happy?

563
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:32,240
Mr. Ye?

564
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:34,880
Have a seat.

565
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:37,560
Call me Richard.

566
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:40,360
Or, as your company does,
don't use an English name.

567
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,640
Call me Ye Xinzhi.

568
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,280
Just drop the "Mr." stuff.

569
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:49,000
In the CBD, if you shout that,
four out of ten people will turn around.

570
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,280
Hi. A beer, please.

571
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:53,440
Sure thing, sir.

572
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:55,240
-I'll have another one too.
-Got it.

573
00:36:00,320 --> 00:36:01,320
Thanks.

574
00:36:03,560 --> 00:36:06,440
Off work this early and so thrilled?
Did you pull off a coup or something?

575
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:11,840
After all this time at Maxmise,
I finally get to lead a project on my own.

576
00:36:15,960 --> 00:36:17,920
Got a promotion? A raise?

577
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Did your probation end early?

578
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:24,080
Wipe that smug look off your face.

579
00:36:24,160 --> 00:36:26,640
Lots of people
from nearby offices eat here.

580
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:27,640
The consulting world is small.

581
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:31,480
If someone saw you
looking like you just got revenge,

582
00:36:32,080 --> 00:36:34,280
and it ended up online…

583
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:39,840
Last time you told me to watch my back,
and now you're calling me out.

584
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,400
Drop the preachy attitude.
It's a real turn-off.

585
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:45,000
I hear you. Not changing a thing.

586
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:51,760
You seem pretty happy too.

587
00:36:52,720 --> 00:36:54,600
Of course. I just closed a deal.

588
00:36:54,680 --> 00:36:56,600
Tianhe Air brand transformation project.

589
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:58,840
What? Jealous?

590
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:02,760
When will I ever get to where you are?

591
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:04,600
When?

592
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:06,840
When you get smile lines,
bags under your eyes,

593
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:10,120
and no amount
of cosmetic procedures can fix them.

594
00:37:14,720 --> 00:37:17,360
Why are you staring at me? I age well.

595
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:25,280
Anyway, congratulations.

596
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,440
And thank you

597
00:37:29,040 --> 00:37:30,360
for the other day.

598
00:37:30,440 --> 00:37:32,840
Your guidance and advice
have been invaluable to me.

599
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:37,560
Let me put it plainly.
Thank you. Thank you, sir.

600
00:37:38,320 --> 00:37:42,240
Please, don't call me "sir."
And can you not toast me like that?

601
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:51,840
-Alright.
-Cheers.

602
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:52,960
Cheers.

603
00:37:58,040 --> 00:37:59,000
By the way,

604
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:02,880
knowing how to dine with clients
and pick restaurants is also a skill.

605
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,360
French food takes too long.

606
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:06,440
Chinese food has too many
dietary restrictions.

607
00:38:06,520 --> 00:38:09,160
Italian food? Just wait
till you're on business trips.

608
00:38:09,240 --> 00:38:11,800
Room service spaghetti bolognese
is gonna be all you ever eat.

609
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:14,280
Try to avoid Japanese food

610
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:17,440
because in Japanese culture,
men inherently come before women.

611
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:20,760
The atmosphere affects how much a client
trusts and respects you.

612
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:22,560
So what kind of place should I go to?

613
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:24,040
Coffee shops.

614
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:25,440
Fast. Efficient.

615
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:27,360
Standardized service.
Talk business, then leave.

616
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:28,800
No drinking. No picking anyone up.

617
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:33,280
Also, never pour coffee or tea
for anyone at the office.

618
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:35,200
Because you're not a waitress. You're a…

619
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,520
Consultant.

620
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:39,040
Right now, you're just an intern analyst.

621
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:42,280
Above you are senior analysts
and associate consultants.

622
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:46,320
It'll take you at least two years
to make consultant.

623
00:38:46,400 --> 00:38:48,320
Well, I came here for that goal.

624
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:53,040
Then I wish you success.
Maxmise's elimination rate is brutal.

625
00:38:53,720 --> 00:38:55,120
You've got something
to say about everything.

626
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,760
One minute you're putting me down,
the next you're encouraging me.

627
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:57,920
One minute you have me
pouring you a drink,

628
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,320
the next you tell me to maintain dignity.

629
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:02,560
I was your interviewer.

630
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:03,680
That's different.

631
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:09,360
So as my interviewer,

632
00:39:09,440 --> 00:39:12,400
teach me how to land
a big deal like Tianhe.

633
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,520
Good question.

634
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:15,760
Our firms are competitors.

635
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:17,760
That's confidential.
Can I just tell you that?

636
00:39:18,360 --> 00:39:20,040
Then why did you teach me
how to pick restaurants?

637
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:22,280
Most people don't need to be taught that.

638
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:23,320
It's common sense.

639
00:39:57,200 --> 00:39:58,280
Richard.

640
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:00,520
Right away.

641
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:03,040
Then I wish you continued success.

642
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:04,560
And that you buy back
your mother's old apartment soon.

643
00:40:05,160 --> 00:40:06,400
Get what you came for.

644
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:32,240
Congratulations. You got what you wanted.

645
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:34,080
Still, be careful.

646
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:35,440
Take care of yourself.
